# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project settings
# (Project Settings -> API). Both values are safe to expose to the browser —
# row-level security is what protects the data, not the key.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase is migrating "anon" -> "publishable". The app reads ANON_KEY first
# and falls back to PUBLISHABLE_KEY (see src/proxy.ts), so setting either works.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key

# Never put the service_role key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable — it bypasses RLS.

# Server-only. Required by /api/custom-planes, which is the sole write path for
# custom planes: it runs the NSFW scan and then writes with a client that
# bypasses RLS. Without it, plane creation returns a 500.
# Supabase is renaming "service_role" -> "secret"; either name is read.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key
